  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A net torque acts on a horizontal disk of mass 0.20 kg and radius 0.40 m that is initially at rest. The disk begins to rotate. The graph shows the variation with time t of the angular speed ω of the disk.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The moment of inertia of a disk of mass M and radius R about a vertical axis through its centre is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>MR<sup>2</sup>.</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Show that the angular acceleration of the disk is about 6 rad s<sup>−2</sup>. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Calculate the torque that acts on the disk while it accelerates. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> </p><p>While the disk is rotating at its final constant angular speed, a small object of mass 0.10 kg falls on the disk and sticks to the edge of the disk.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p><p></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c.i\"><p><strong>c.i</strong> Calculate the new angular speed of the disk. [3]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c.ii\"><p><strong>c.ii</strong> Determine the fraction of the total energy of the disk that was lost. [3]</p></section>"
  },
